All MUST-SHOW items render and no MUST-NOT-SHOW item appears; no P1. The neutral ramp is coherent and most text sits between 7:1 and 19:1, but every state that is encoded as a small mark or a tinted pill is where this theme thins out.

Changes: (1) landed — the provenance sentences set flush-left at x1158, exactly the label-column edge — but the `#c8c8c8` row rule that separates every other metadata row now falls at y246 *between* the DATA badge and its own sentences, and there is no rule above DATA. (4) landed: exactly one `⊙` (x76–81, y380–386) and one `⊘` (x75–82, y310–316). (5) landed (`← demo`). (2) is not verifiable here — no `COST · TRANSACTIONFEE` row exists in this fixture; `COST · MANA 88000 / 200000` is the only cost row. (3) is not verifiable here — this view has no decoded-input note.

Glyph verdict, measured: `⊘` is #484848 on white — 9.15:1 core, 3.59:1 flanks. `⊙` is #0e7490 on the #a5f3fc band — 4.29:1 at its four caps and centre dot, but the ring flanks (#43a1b6, #4ba7bc) measure 2.40:1 and 2.23:1. The previous round's 2.40:1 is *unchanged*; only the caps improved. Centroid-aligned ink maps differ by 7.6px of ~33px mean ink (23%), all inside a 4×4px interior. Desaturated at 1× they are one smudged ring, separating only above 4×, and they never share a surface. Not distinguishable without colour.

Fixes: fill `⊙`'s centre and take its stroke to ≥3:1 on the band; move the y246 rule above DATA.

